    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d876">

                <pb facs="0800" n="684" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg684"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 882.51/422.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Monrovia</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 31, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s July 19. Under bank agreement, Erlanger’s interest for current
                    quarter will be advanced to Sharp August 15 for immediate transmission. Clark
                    urges that bankers arrange with Erlanger to hold advance here, or, failing this,
                    he be permitted to <pb facs="0801" n="685" xml:id="pg685"/> offset payment
                    against interest on new loan. Receivership crippled if Liberian Government
                    forced to pay double interest. Ready money imperatively needed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chum.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
